From 501968b46b2bb85e517f225712003fc3ebb49db8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: memra-lane <lane@localhost>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 14:40:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] dsv4 serve: gate-only door to raise the prefill width
 ceiling from 64 to the kernel's 512

The served MEMRA_DSV4_PREFILL_CHUNK ceiling is DSV4_SERVING_BATCH_WIDTH_MAX = 64 while the
kernel's is DSV4_BATCH_WIDTH_MAX = 512. Both constants entered together in 8a52da7c7 (#318):
512 was qualified for the bring-up surface and serving kept 64.

This matters because prefill, not decode, is where a served request spends its GPU seconds at
this family's real traffic shape (44:1 to 70:1 input:output), and prefill throughput is set by
the chunk width. dsv4_wide_prefill_gate already checks widths 32/128/512 byte-exact against each
other over logits, every live cache class, DSpark rings and sampled speculative output, in both
grouped arms, so the wider widths are not unqualified numerics: they are unqualified for the
serving surface specifically.

MEMRA_DSV4_SERVE_WIDE_PREFILL=1 raises the accepted ceiling to the kernel's. Default is unset,
which keeps 64. Nothing else changes: the launcher still picks the chunk, MEMRA_CTX still bounds
it, and a width above the kernel's is still refused at boot. The [dsv4-serve] boot line now
prints prefill-width-ceiling N so a receipt can name the arm that ran.

Both arms plus the red arm (door OFF must still refuse 128) are unit-gated in
prefill_chunk_flag_tests::wide_prefill_door_has_two_arms. The FLAGS.md row lands here with the
default, both arms, the rollback seam, the decide-by date (2026-09-24) and the receipt pointer.

Signed-off-by: memra-lane <lane@localhost>
---
 crates/memra-server/src/dsv4_serve.rs | 86 +++++++++++++++++++++++----
 docs/FLAGS.md                         |  1 +
 2 files changed, 75 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/memra-server/src/dsv4_serve.rs b/crates/memra-server/src/dsv4_serve.rs
